# Gym Pages

Full overview and phasing: @docs/gym-pages.md. That file is the source of truth; read it before designing or building anything for gyms.

Key points to keep in mind:

- Build in phases. V1 is standalone public gym pages (info, equipment, policies, amenities, discipline checklists, attribution/freshness, chain templates, member editing). Logger/AI integration is V2, community/owners is V3. Do not build later phases early.
- Equipment items have three states: unknown (default), present, absent.
- Data is reports with attribution and last-confirmed date; wording must be honest ("lifters report...").
- Public pages are server-rendered HTTP and indexable. Mutations go through WebSocket handlers.
- Follow `gainz2.mdc` architecture: logic in `services.py`, models only (user runs migrations).
- If the design changes, update `docs/gym-pages.md`.
